  "version": 1,
  "title": "Ray-Chaudhuri–Wilson: uniform families with restricted intersections",
  "abstract": "Formalizes Theorem 3 of On t-designs (1975): a k-uniform family of subsets of an n-element ground set whose distinct-pair intersection sizes lie in L ⊆ {0,...,k−1} has at most binomial(n,|L|) members. Includes the actual-intersection-spectrum formulation, the uniform one-intersection bound, and equality examples consisting of all s-subsets.",
